  "jd_text": "Manager of Applied AI Architecture, Partnerships\nSan Francisco, CA | New York City, NY | Seattle, WA\n\nAbout Anthropic\n\nAnthropic's mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.\n\nAbout the role\n\nAs the Manager of the Partnerships Applied AI Solutions Architect team, you will drive adoption of frontier AI by enabling deployment of Anthropic's products (Claude for Enterprise, Claude Code, API) through our Global and Regional System Integrators, cloud partners (AWS, GCP, Azure), and strategic technology partners.\n\nYou will build and lead a team of Partner Solutions Architects, establish processes and best practices for partner-led pre-sales engagements, and represent Anthropic as the technical lead on its most important partnerships. In collaboration with Sales, Partnerships, Product, and Engineering, you will help partners incorporate leading-edge AI into their practices, accelerate indirect revenue, and execute long-term GTM strategy while maintaining our best-in-class safety standards.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n    Team Leadership & Development: Hire, manage, and mentor a team of Partner Solutions Architects. Set goals, run reviews, and coach each team member toward high productivity and career growth.\n    Strategic Technical Partnership: Act as the senior technical thought partner to Anthropic's GTM partnerships team. Co-build partner strategy with aligned GTM leadership, drive key programs, and align cross-functional stakeholders (Sales, Product, Engineering) behind partner outcomes.\n    Partner Enablement & Ecosystem: Embed your team with GSI and cloud partner technical teams to enable their AI practices, troubleshoot, and evangelize Anthropic in their developer communities. Represent Anthropic at partner events (GSI workshops, AWS/GCP summits, hackathons) and contribute technical content and thought leadership.\n    Joint Solution Development: Lead partners in identifying high-value, industry-specific GenAI applications. Develop joint solutions and codify reference architectures and best practices to accelerate time to deployment.\n    Customer Deal Support: Own the technical portion of partner-led pre-sales engagements. Intervene directly on strategic deals where partners are the primary delivery vehicle, providing deep solution architecture guidance.\n    Product Feedback: Gather and validate feedback on Anthropic's products from partner deployments and deliver it to Product and Engineering to inform roadmap and partner strategy.\n\nYou may be a good fit if you have\n\n    7+ years in technical customer-facing or partner-facing roles (Solutions Architect, Sales Engineer, Partner SE, TAM).\n    3+ years managing pre-sales or partner-facing technical teams; comfortable building foundational teams in ambiguous, fast-moving environments.\n    Track record building and scaling partnerships with GSIs (e.g., Accenture, Deloitte, TCS, Infosys) and/or cloud providers (AWS, GCP, Azure).\n    Deep understanding of partner-led selling and delivery: indirect revenue models, enablement at scale, and joint GTM motions.\n    Technical depth in enterprise AI deployments: LLM architecture, prompt engineering, evaluation, API integrations, and production use cases.\n    Exceptional communication and executive presence; able to build trusted relationships with C-suite, partner leadership, and engineering teams alike.\n    A love of teaching and mentoring, and a passion for advancing safe, beneficial AI.\n\nStrong candidates may also have\n\n    5+ years leading partner-facing SA teams through hypergrowth, including developing both senior and junior talent.\n    Direct experience helping GSIs or consultancies build their AI/ML practice - enablement programs, certification paths, joint solution development.\n\nCompensation\n\nThe annual compensation range for this role is listed below.\n\nFor sales roles, the range provided is the role's On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.\n\nAnnual Salary: $315,000 - $380,000 USD\n[# APPS_RG_EXEC_SUMMARY_TARGETING_CAP targeting-only; not proof]\n",
  "briefing": "# Anthropic - Manager of Applied AI Architecture, Partnerships briefing packet\n| Manager of Applied AI Architecture, Partnerships | $315,000\u2013$380,000 OTE | Reports to Partnerships (enterprise partner GTM) |\n\n## JD Complement\nAnthropic\u2019s partnership architecture function sits where frontier-model capabilities meet enterprise delivery reality.\nThe core challenge is converting partner access to Claude into governed, repeatable customer outcomes across\ncomplex organizations.\n\nThis requires balancing expansion with consistency. As external delivery organizations bring Claude into more\naccounts, technical quality, security expectations, adoption practices, and field learning must remain coherent\nrather than varying materially by partner or region.\n\nThe role is likely consequential because it connects ecosystem scale with the practical details that determine\nwhether customers realize value after evaluation: implementation design, workflow adoption, controls, and\noperational readiness.\n\n## Company DNA & Operating Model\nAnthropic is a frontier AI company centered on Claude and structured as a public benefit corporation. Its stated\nidentity emphasizes dependable AI behavior, interpretability, steerability, and responsible development.\n\nIts market presence spans business teams, developers, and enterprise technology organizations. Claude is\npositioned for knowledge work, analysis, software work, and complex problem solving, creating a product surface\nthat can enter an organization through multiple technical and business pathways.\n\nThis creates a commercial model in which product capability alone is insufficient. Enterprise value depends on\nhow customers connect tools to workflows, establish appropriate controls, prepare users, and expand successful\npatterns without losing confidence in the technology.\n\n## Company Strategy & Operating Pressure\nAnthropic must support several routes into an enterprise at once: broad employee usage, developer integration,\nand software-focused workflows. These routes may involve distinct sponsors, budgets, control requirements,\nimplementation teams, and measures of success.\n\nEnterprise adoption guidance frames deployment as an ongoing operating journey. Technical setup is paired with\nlaunch planning, organizational change, education, and broader usage expansion. That framing makes the quality\nof customer delivery a strategic issue rather than a downstream services concern.\n\nFor the ecosystem, the pressure is to make partners capable of delivering credible outcomes at scale while\nkeeping customer feedback useful. Raw field anecdotes are less valuable than structured evidence about recurring\nrequirements, integration friction, governance needs, and observed adoption barriers.\n\n## Leadership & Stakeholder Map\nPartner architecture operates across a broad set of internal and external decision makers. Success likely depends\non establishing shared technical standards without creating unnecessary friction for commercial teams or partners.\n\n- Cloud, technology, and services firms need clear paths from product familiarity to delivery capability.\n\nAnthropic\u2019s January 2026 introduction of Labs, associated in research with Mike Krieger, signals continuing\norganizational evolution around product innovation. That environment increases the value of teams that can\ntranslate changing capabilities into clear partner-facing practices.\n\n## AI, Data, Platform, Architecture Signals\nClaude is presented as an AI assistant designed around safety, accuracy, and security, with support for analysis,\nwriting, coding, and difficult business problems. In that context, architecture is part of the value proposition:\ncustomers need confidence not only in model performance, but also in how capabilities fit their environment.\n\nClaude Enterprise includes security, compliance, and administration features for both business and developer\naudiences. Administrator materials also address Claude Code seat configuration, indicating that governance may\nneed to span general employee use and technical-builder use within the same organization.\n\nThe resulting architecture agenda is broader than API connectivity. It includes controlled access, role design,\nimplementation sequencing, workflow integration, enablement, measurement, and expansion planning. Reusable\npatterns must be technically credible for enterprise IT while remaining understandable to sponsors and delivery\nteams.\n\n## Partnership / Ecosystem Motion\nAnthropic describes cloud, technology, and services partners as important routes for addressing customer AI\nchallenges. This suggests an ecosystem model built around joint customer outcomes rather than simple lead sharing.\n\nEach partner type brings a distinct scaling mechanism. Cloud providers can influence infrastructure and\nprocurement paths; technology firms can embed Claude within adjacent product contexts; services organizations\ncan provide implementation capacity, industry knowledge, and organizational-change support.\n\nThe critical operating unit is likely the reusable joint offering: a defined customer problem, reference design,\ndelivery approach, governance model, enablement package, and path from initial interest to sustained use.\n\n- Partner education must create practical delivery competence, not only product familiarity or sales awareness.\n\n## Recent Events & Urgency\nAnthropic\u2019s Labs introduction in January 2026 indicates continued movement in its product and innovation\norganization. Meanwhile, its enterprise materials emphasize adoption beyond initial technical activation.\n\nTogether, these signals create urgency for a strong partner architecture capability. Product evolution may move\nfaster than partner practices, while large customers expect external advisors to translate new functionality into\nsecure, understandable, and operationally viable deployments.\n\nCompetitive conditions in enterprise AI heighten this need. Differentiation is experienced through customer\nimplementation: whether teams can use the product effectively, whether governance is workable, and whether\npartners can turn technical promise into sustained business value.\n\n## apps_rg Positioning Themes (targeting only, not proof)\n- Designing enablement systems for cloud, consulting, and technology ecosystems.\n- Converting customer problems into reusable solution patterns, reference designs, and rollout playbooks.\n- Connecting enterprise architecture, governance, security, and organizational adoption.\n- Establishing evidence-based feedback mechanisms between field delivery and product development.\n- Leading across partnerships, commercial teams, engineering, product, and customer technology organizations.\n- Creating operating discipline for indirect growth in fast-changing technical environments.\n- Combining technical depth with executive communication, coaching, and ecosystem influence.\n\n## apps_lic Outreach Angles (targeting only, not proof)\n- Anthropic frames enterprise success as sustained adoption rather than a one-time implementation milestone.\n- The ecosystem opportunity is to make Claude delivery more repeatable across varied customer environments.\n- Cloud, services, and technology partners require different forms of technical readiness and operating support.\n- Enterprise usage spans business teams and developers, increasing the importance of coordinated governance.\n- Joint offerings can package partner expertise into credible, reusable routes to customer value.\n- Structured learning from delivery teams can help separate broad product needs from isolated account requests.\n- Anthropic\u2019s responsible-AI identity makes deployment quality a commercial and reputational consideration.\n\n## Do Not Use As Proof\nThe JD and this briefing are targeting inputs only. Candidate claims, outcomes, scope, leadership, technical depth,\nand partnership results must come from the governed resume/proof graph.\n[# APPS_RG_EXEC_SUMMARY_TARGETING_CAP targeting-only; not proof]\n",
